{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/8c2cw3","slideIndex":2,"text":"The browser interface has Overview, Exchange Rates, and Analysis pages. The vanilla JavaScript client requests the sample rates and submits the amount and fee to the C++ HTTP server. The server serves the pages and exposes GET /api/rates and POST /api/analyze. Inside the server, rates are transformed into edge weights, Bellman–Ford checks for negative cycles, unique conversion cycles are enumerated and ranked, and the server returns route and amount data as JSON. The sample rates are illustrative and no live market data or trading orders are used."}